1
00:00:12,700 --> 00:00:13,800
(Let it go.)

2
00:00:43,724 --> 00:00:45,964
=Revenge From A Wife=

3
00:00:46,091 --> 00:00:48,317
=Episode 1=

4
00:00:48,800 --> 00:00:50,561
(To reclaim your chastity,)

5
00:00:51,001 --> 00:00:53,201
(first endure the pain of torn flesh.)

6
00:00:53,881 --> 00:00:55,921
(To restore your maidenhood,)

7
00:00:56,720 --> 00:00:59,800
(you must endure a heart-rending trial.)

8
00:01:03,760 --> 00:01:05,521
(I was a commoner outside the capital.)

9
00:01:06,440 --> 00:01:08,121
(My husband and I had only each other.)

10
00:01:09,041 --> 00:01:11,001
(His skills got him into the palace.)

11
00:01:12,160 --> 00:01:13,360
(When he returned,)

12
00:01:14,401 --> 00:01:16,201
(only half his mangled body remained.)

13
00:01:17,800 --> 00:01:19,281
(This world made a monster of me.)

14
00:01:19,921 --> 00:01:21,201
(I had nowhere left to turn.)

15
00:01:22,240 --> 00:01:23,600
(My husband Shouhe)

16
00:01:24,240 --> 00:01:25,481
(endured such agony.)

17
00:01:26,201 --> 00:01:27,440
(I swear to repay it in blood.)

18
00:01:29,270 --> 00:01:31,163
(Seven days earlier)

19
00:01:33,347 --> 00:01:35,287
(Su Wanniang, Chen Shouhe's Wife)

20
00:01:36,440 --> 00:01:37,561
(By my count,)

21
00:01:37,960 --> 00:01:39,240
(your father will be home soon.)

22
00:01:40,001 --> 00:01:40,921
Shouhe.

23
00:01:46,960 --> 00:01:47,960
Madam.

24
00:01:48,440 --> 00:01:50,641
Your husband had an accident at court.

25
00:01:51,001 --> 00:01:52,360
A noble at court showed mercy

26
00:01:52,681 --> 00:01:54,240
and sent his body home for burial.

27
00:01:54,720 --> 00:01:56,440
He was an exceptional craftsman.

28
00:01:56,440 --> 00:01:58,041
His Majesty greatly admired his work.

29
00:01:58,481 --> 00:02:01,201
His final work
is kept in Guizhen Cottage.

30
00:02:01,320 --> 00:02:03,201
This reward is from the palace.

31
00:02:03,561 --> 00:02:04,561
My condolences.

32
00:02:33,720 --> 00:02:38,841
♪I sing a folk song to the passing wind♪

33
00:02:38,920 --> 00:02:43,440
♪I sing only for you♪
(Chen Shouhe, Su Wanniang's Husband)

34
00:02:43,440 --> 00:02:44,160
Wanniang.

35
00:02:44,160 --> 00:02:45,160
♪We...♪

36
00:02:45,160 --> 00:02:46,401
If you keep singing,

37
00:02:47,200 --> 00:02:48,200
I won't want to leave.

38
00:02:57,880 --> 00:02:58,841
Once this palace job is done

39
00:02:59,281 --> 00:03:00,320
and I get paid,

40
00:03:01,160 --> 00:03:02,681
I'll buy you a fur collar

41
00:03:03,401 --> 00:03:04,241
to keep your throat warm.

42
00:03:05,040 --> 00:03:06,600
Those are for wealthy families.

43
00:03:07,160 --> 00:03:08,281
Let's not spend money on that.

44
00:03:10,320 --> 00:03:10,920
Wanniang.

45
00:03:12,320 --> 00:03:13,001
If others can have one,

46
00:03:13,720 --> 00:03:14,440
so can you.

47
00:03:16,241 --> 00:03:16,920
All right.

48
00:03:17,320 --> 00:03:18,361
Then we'll do it your way.

49
00:03:33,320 --> 00:03:33,920
Wanniang.

50
00:03:34,640 --> 00:03:35,401
Wait for me.

51
00:03:36,760 --> 00:03:37,720
Come back soon.

52
00:03:44,681 --> 00:03:46,200
His Majesty has called for thrift.

53
00:03:46,920 --> 00:03:47,640
So I

54
00:03:47,961 --> 00:03:49,320
had this woven from grass.

55
00:03:49,841 --> 00:03:51,040
It may be common grass,

56
00:03:51,720 --> 00:03:53,401
but it still has to look refined.

57
00:03:54,040 --> 00:03:55,200
It must be crafted

58
00:03:55,561 --> 00:03:56,961
(Consort Chen, Late Empress's Sister)
even finer than

59
00:03:57,160 --> 00:03:58,640
embroidery.

60
00:03:59,200 --> 00:04:00,440
(Consort Shu)
How ingenious, Your Highness.

61
00:04:00,440 --> 00:04:02,961
Which artisan made it?

62
00:04:05,880 --> 00:04:07,081
I'm Chen Shouhe.

63
00:04:07,841 --> 00:04:08,561
Greetings, Your Highness.

64
00:04:08,841 --> 00:04:10,600
This dragon's head

65
00:04:11,081 --> 00:04:12,480
is hard to weave tightly.

66
00:04:12,720 --> 00:04:13,480
How did you

67
00:04:14,001 --> 00:04:15,040
get it this tight?

68
00:04:15,320 --> 00:04:16,081
Your Highness,

69
00:04:16,600 --> 00:04:18,081
there's a grass called

70
00:04:18,241 --> 00:04:19,161
Dragon's Beard Grass.

71
00:04:19,400 --> 00:04:20,080
If you weave

72
00:04:20,760 --> 00:04:22,681
two shoots from the same root together,

73
00:04:22,880 --> 00:04:23,721
the weave will hold.

74
00:04:23,960 --> 00:04:25,041
The same root?

75
00:04:25,161 --> 00:04:25,640
Yes.

76
00:04:25,760 --> 00:04:26,721
They must share the same root.

77
00:04:27,161 --> 00:04:28,041
A single shoot won't do.

78
00:04:28,361 --> 00:04:29,361
If a single shoot

79
00:04:29,681 --> 00:04:30,801
isn't paired with another

80
00:04:30,960 --> 00:04:32,121
from the same root,

81
00:04:32,440 --> 00:04:33,840
you can still weave it in,

82
00:04:34,561 --> 00:04:35,041
but it

83
00:04:35,721 --> 00:04:36,721
won't hold for long.

84
00:04:38,960 --> 00:04:39,681
You may

85
00:04:40,440 --> 00:04:41,280
rise.

86
00:04:42,001 --> 00:04:43,721
Just wait for your reward.

87
00:04:45,960 --> 00:04:47,041
Thank you, Your Highness.

88
00:04:57,520 --> 00:04:57,960
Your Highness,

89
00:04:58,361 --> 00:04:59,161
I don't know

90
00:04:59,801 --> 00:05:00,601
what crime I committed.

91
00:05:01,161 --> 00:05:02,481
It's been years

92
00:05:02,760 --> 00:05:05,721
since anyone in this palace reminded me

93
00:05:06,361 --> 00:05:09,241
I had a sister who shared the same root.

94
00:05:10,041 --> 00:05:11,121
She and I

95
00:05:11,561 --> 00:05:12,840
shared the same father

96
00:05:13,200 --> 00:05:14,481
and even the same face.

97
00:05:15,041 --> 00:05:16,320
She was the legitimate daughter

98
00:05:17,001 --> 00:05:18,041
and became Empress.

99
00:05:19,121 --> 00:05:20,200
But me?

100
00:05:20,361 --> 00:05:21,721
I was a concubine's daughter.

101
00:05:23,400 --> 00:05:24,601
With only a face

102
00:05:25,121 --> 00:05:27,200
that resembled hers,

103
00:05:28,280 --> 00:05:30,520
I could only become a consort.

104
00:05:31,241 --> 00:05:33,041
You said one shoot wouldn't last.

105
00:05:33,440 --> 00:05:34,601
But she's dead,

106
00:05:34,960 --> 00:05:36,320
while I'm still alive and well.

107
00:05:36,601 --> 00:05:37,721
That's not what I meant.

108
00:05:38,280 --> 00:05:39,121
Please show mercy, Your Highness!

109
00:05:39,241 --> 00:05:40,001
Please show mercy, Your Highness!

110
00:05:40,200 --> 00:05:41,001
Please show mercy, Your Highness!

111
00:05:41,601 --> 00:05:43,241
How dare a lowly grass weaver

112
00:05:43,561 --> 00:05:44,760
talk back to Her Highness?

113
00:05:45,280 --> 00:05:46,280
What are you waiting for?

114
00:05:47,241 --> 00:05:47,760
Your Highness!

115
00:05:48,481 --> 00:05:48,960
I...

116
00:05:49,520 --> 00:05:51,161
My wife is waiting for me at home.

117
00:05:52,721 --> 00:05:54,280
Please show mercy, Your Highness!

118
00:05:54,840 --> 00:05:56,320
Let's see...

119
00:05:56,320 --> 00:05:57,320
Please show mercy, Your Highness!

120
00:05:57,481 --> 00:05:59,121
How long a man cut off at the root

121
00:05:59,721 --> 00:06:01,400
can hold out.

122
00:06:24,241 --> 00:06:25,840
Shouhe!

123
00:06:30,481 --> 00:06:32,361
Shouhe!

124
00:06:53,489 --> 00:06:57,676
♪Sunset fades beyond the lonely city♪

125
00:06:57,810 --> 00:07:01,423
♪Dusk snow paints the green hills♪

126
00:07:01,658 --> 00:07:04,257
♪A lone rider storms the old pass♪

127
00:07:04,294 --> 00:07:06,574
♪Drunk, I gaze by lamplight♪

128
00:07:06,621 --> 00:07:10,450
♪Old friends have all drifted away♪

129
00:07:10,852 --> 00:07:14,205
♪My broken sword rusts, as do I♪

130
00:07:15,132 --> 00:07:18,645
♪Jackdaws cry into the night♪

131
00:07:19,145 --> 00:07:21,712
♪Half a banner snaps in the wind♪

132
00:07:21,838 --> 00:07:23,871
♪In dreams, I return to the camps♪

133
00:07:23,938 --> 00:07:27,715
♪Moonlight chills my armor♪

134
00:07:28,065 --> 00:07:32,398
♪Life is a dream through many winters♪

135
00:07:32,621 --> 00:07:36,128
♪I gaze beyond the edge of the world♪

136
00:07:36,309 --> 00:07:39,162
♪Parting sorrow spills across the moon♪

137
00:07:39,229 --> 00:07:44,843
♪The moon and wind mean nothing now♪

138
00:07:44,883 --> 00:07:47,897
♪History turns to ash before ink dries♪

139
00:07:47,938 --> 00:07:53,946
♪Who plays the zither
and sighs at the pavilion?♪

140
00:07:54,613 --> 00:08:01,568
♪The past has faded away♪

141
00:08:01,568 --> 00:08:05,600
♪The past has faded away♪
